# Enterprise Knowledge Graph Extraction Benchmark (KGEB)

KGEB evaluates entity and relation extraction methods on semi-structured enterprise text. It ships a reproducible pipeline, schemas, gold annotations, and an evaluation framework.

## Features
- 🔍 **Entity extraction** for 10 enterprise entity types (see `entities.json`).
- 🔗 **Relation extraction** for 30 predefined relation types (see `relations.json`).
- 📊 **Evaluation**: precision/recall/F1, schema compliance, logical consistency.
- 🧪 **Automated tests**: extraction correctness, conflict handling, multi-document support.
- 🐳 **Reproducible env**: `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile`, `setup.sh`, one-click `run_tests` scripts.

## Quickstart
```bash
# optional: create venv
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .[dev]

# run extraction
kgeb run --documents documents.txt --entities-schema entities.json --relations-schema relations.json \
	--entities-output entities_output.json --relations-output relations_output.json

# evaluate against gold
kgeb evaluate --pred-entities entities_output.json --pred-relations relations_output.json \
	--gold-entities data/gold/entities_output.json --gold-relations data/gold/relations_output.json \
	--entities-schema entities.json

# run tests
./run_tests.sh  # or run_tests.bat on Windows
```

## Project Structure
- `kgeb/` – core extraction & evaluation code
- `entities.json` – entity schema
- `relations.json` – relation schema (30 types)
- `documents.txt` – sample corpus
- `data/gold/` – gold annotations (generated)
- `tests/` – pytest suite
- `Dockerfile`, `requirements.txt`, `setup.sh`, `run_tests.*` – reproducibility

